I've met two chameleon liches in recent memory. One killed a promising
rogue in the first level of the quest without giving me any time to
react (note to self: *never* go to rogue's quest without magic
resistance or a ring of protection from shape changers). The second
one spent its first turn to summon nasties so I had time to burn the
E-word and read a scroll of earth to help me survive until it changed
into some easier form. I was very lucky in that all summoned nasties
respected the E-word, otherwise I would have been dead, dead, dead,
since it was still early in the game.

But anyway, touches of death are so rare that you don't really have to
take special precautions for them. Wands of lightning blowing up wands
and rings is a more probable threat, and a good reason for obtaining
reflection as quickly as possible. 

